<title>INDIA: Raytheon wins $60 mln India contract.</title>
<headline>Raytheon wins $60 mln India contract.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Engineers and Contractors, a unit of Raytheon Co, said on Wednesday it had won a $60 million engineering service contract to set up a coke facility and a related power plant in India.</p>
<p>The plant will be for India's Bellary Coke and Power Ltd in the southern Indian state of Tamil Nadu, the statement said. &quot;The $60 million contract is one of the three projects worth $270 million that the company has won in the United States and India,&quot; the statement added.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom, +91-11-301 2024</p>
